ction. The bad deploy was v2.3.1, which was failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** us-east, us-west and eu-west are all now on v2.3.0. Afterwards the service reports healthy and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api, which paged on-call. It describes the failure, the rollback and the current health, and notes that the cause of the v2.3.1 failure still needs to be found before it's deployed again.\n\nThe deploy history shows that v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging, so it was promoted to production despite failing there. That may be worth raising in the incident review.", "type": "text"}]}]}